  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.62,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings level off at about 0.60–0.65 from 5 h onward. I diluted retained aliquots to check whether this was a real plateau or the reader saturating. Diluted readings corrected back to undiluted: 18 h at 4x read 0.1513 and 0.1514, which gives 0.605, the same as the undiluted 0.605. 18 h at 10x read 0.0631 and 0.0673, which gives 0.652, about 8% higher. That gap is small, the two readings vary by about ±0.002 (about ±0.02 after correction), and the 4x result doesn't show the same gap. 15 h at 4x read 0.1592 and 0.1507, which gives 0.62, against 0.602 undiluted. So the reader responds proportionally across dilutions, and corrected values stay near 0.60–0.65 rather than rising above the plateau. If the reader were saturating, the corrected diluted values would be clearly higher than the undiluted readings. This means the late plateau is real stationary-phase biomass at about the level read (OD around 0.6–0.65). My best estimate at 18 h is about 0.62. A small reader non-linearity, at most about 8%, can't be fully ruled out with the six readings the budget allowed."
  },
